class.description:
A [FlowGraphPlayer] is a thin node around a [FlowGraphPlayback] (like [AnimationPlayer] around its animations): it plays [member graph], optionally when it is ready ([member autostart]), drives waiting nodes from the scene tree and repeats all signals of the playback. Use [method get_playback] for everything else (choices, travel, variables, save and restore).
[b]Processing.[/b] The player processes only while the current node waits through [method FlowNode._process_waiting] (for example a [FlowWaitNode]); an idle player, or one that waits for the game (a dialog line, a signal), costs nothing per frame. [member callback_mode_process] chooses the physics or the idle frame; in [constant CALLBACK_MODE_PROCESS_MANUAL], call [method FlowGraphPlayback.process] yourself. Pausing follows [member Node.process_mode].
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
@onready var player: FlowGraphPlayer = $FlowGraphPlayer
@onready var label: Label = $Label

func _ready():
    player.node_entered.connect(func(id, node): label.text = node.get_title())
    player.finished.connect(func(end_id): label.text = "Done")
    player.play()
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public override void _Ready()
{
    var player = GetNode<FlowGraphPlayer>("FlowGraphPlayer");
    var label = GetNode<Label>("Label");
    player.NodeEntered += (id, node) => label.Text = node.GetTitle();
    player.Finished += endId => label.Text = "Done";
    player.Play();
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
